  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nThe central idea is to use multi-modal optimization with pattern perturbation and geographic optimization to escape local minima. Unlike grid upscaling, this approach generates diverse candidates by combining moves of different costs and optimizing phasik transitions. It directly minimizes the overlap integral using adaptive resolution allocation, rather than relying on fixed interpolation. The method utilizes the gradient information to compute energy landscape features, enabling directional grid adjustments where the trade-off between resolution and objective improvement is most favorable.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\nVariables: h(x) \u2208 [0,1] over [0,2] with \u222bh(x)dx=1\nObjective: min(max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx)\nRepresentation: n-point samples uniform over [0,2]\nConstraints: 0\u2264h[i]\u22641, \u2211h[i]=n/2 (discrete)\nOptimization: \n    - Use finite difference gradient with automatic selection based on move cost\n    - SIRecast optimization as linear max-min problem with adaptive penaly values\n    - Compute phase-change energy from gradient features\n    - Project changes through energy landscape analysis\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n3.1 Parent Validation\n    - Verify initial_h_values satisfies: len(h)=n, 0\u2264h[i]\u22641, \u2211h*(2/n)=1\n    - If unavailable, generate random [0,1]-valued vector with normalized integral\n\n3.2 Geographic Phase\n    a) Divide domain into M regions based on gradient features\n    b) For each region: random walk with alpha-stable distribution (shape \u03b1\u22481.5)\n    c) Compute energy gradient = finite-difference excluded volume\n    d) Score regions by probability-distribution intersection\n    e) Preserve top P% performers with fitness density: (energy - mean)/std\n\n3.3 Energy Allocation Phase\n    a) Solve warping equation: \u2211(h(x)-expanded)\u00b2+\u03bb\u222b|\u0394h|dx\n    b) Move particles along potential currents: vx=c\u03ba\u2207E - \u03b7(\u2207E)\n    c) Apply projection: h_new = clip(project_feasible(h_old + vx*dt), 0,1)\n    d) Score particles by correlation margin: min(1, E_orig/E_new)\n\n3.4 Optimization Loop \n    while time_remaining > 50:\n        3.4.1 Randomly perturb grid points with Cauchy distribution (scale=0.01)\n        3.4.2 Use adaptive gradient descent with momentum (\u03bc=0.9)\n        3.4.3 Apply finite-difference step: max(c*k) new gradient\n        3.4.4 If improvement < tolerance: trigger pattern migration\n                    else: increase grid resolution locally\n\n3.5 Recovery\n    - Clean final solution: project_feasible() with full_local_search\n    - Optimizations constrained by: dx=2/n_bounds, with n_bounds=300,600,900\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n4.1 Core Operations:\n    - Use integer random walks for point selection (p=77% likely)\n    - Apply high-frequency (uniform) perturbations for fine-tuning\n    - Optimize phases with variable cost: high cost for overlap, low cost for resolution\n    - Weight factors by geli\u015fmi\u015fness metric\n\n4.2 Enforcement Rules:\n    - Immediately fallback to L-BFGS for phase failures\n    - Repair solutions using projected descent with analysis 100x faster\n    - Use additional phases if phase times < 30 seconds\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n    - Allocate:\n        Phase 1: 220s for low-cost variations\n        Phase 2: 440s for high-cost optimizations\n        Phase 3: 330s for hybrid enhancements\n    - Disable expensive operators if time < 150s\n    - Use exponential backoff for repetedExceptions\n    - Global safeguard: return updated parent if \u2206E<0.00001 or timeout\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n6.1 Checks:\n    a) Full objective-score metric\n    b) Verify finite values: energ <+inf, correlation vector element-wise >0\n    c) Feasibility constraint satisfaction with fp error <1e-7\n    d) Sanitize candidate: project_feasible() + 10-point local SLSQP to repair bounds\n\n6.2 Procedures:\n    - Generate initial guess from initial_h_values if available\n    - Every 60s checkpoint: evaluate all candidates\n    - Exclude invalid moves: 0<=h_new[i]<=1, \u222b\u2248true\n    - Maintain global best with commitment to lower C5",
